            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mary Rocco"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a very tasty, sweet potatoe recipe without using any sugar. I boiled the potatoes because some review said it took a long time to bake. I mashed them and added the orange juice and raisons and everyone loved it."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MotherLodeViv"
            },
            "reviewBody": "After reading other reviews, I sliced my potatoes thinly and covered the baking dish with foil. That did the trick; the potatoes were very tender, but not mushy after only 45 mins. I also used golden raisins instead of regular raisins. A nice, simple and healthy side dish.",
            "datePublished": "2013-01-24T21:53:09.793Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sam Pstross"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I boiled the potatoes instead of baking them like other reviewers suggested and the texture was perfect. My husband and 1 year-old daughter LOVED this! I actually wasn't a big fan - it tasted too much like candy to me, so I added butter to my portion and it was fine. I made it with chicken tenders and it went well together.",
            "datePublished": "2010-08-30T20:48:24.447Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MrsAmyB"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The flavors were great in this. And I was looking for a good sweet preperation for sweet potatoes without adding all of the marshmallow and brown sugar that make it more like dessert!! But like other reviewers said - the timing was wrong. I ended putting them in the mocrowave for about 5 min to try and get them done after the timing in the oven left them only half cooked. Once they were finished they were delish!",
            "datePublished": "2007-01-29T08:42:37.533Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "KRISTENLC"
            },
            "reviewBody": "instead of orange juice I cut up some oranges and added them. it took longer than 45 minutes, but came out great, especially with a little cinnamon on top.",
            "datePublished": "2004-03-23T21:38:05.437Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
