            },
            "reviewBody": "Just okay. A good healthy recipe, but too orangey for my preference.",
            "datePublished": "2007-01-22T16:30:58.480Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "2"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I followed the directions, and checked the potatoes after 45 minutes. Well, the ones on bottom were somewhat tender, but the ones on top were still firm. So, I had to continually rotate them and even add more orange juice. This is slightly inconvenient, especially since the main dish was already done. They tasted okay, but not good enough to do again.",
            "datePublished": "2002-09-23T18:25:03.107Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe provides a side item with a sweet flavor. Also, it is healthy food, being low-fat with antioxidant-rich sweet potatoes and raisins. I liked the recipe enough to use it twice so far. Thanks, Tali, for sharing this recipe.",
